From 2a1e80944842bf6fd36689bf6bcbb995bf862022 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: x <a@b>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 10:58:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] 0998 vince: do not free the unused end of vm_pages[] with the
 second bank

With vinceram3g=1 the array is sized for the whole span, so its unused end is a few hundred
pages. ml_static_mfree() hands them to the VM while their kernel mappings are still in the pv
lists, and pmap_assert_free() panics when one is reused (0x232ac000). Keep them instead.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UTtYRgmKyxgNh36HwFrzar
---
 osfmk/vm/vm_resident.c | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/osfmk/vm/vm_resident.c b/osfmk/vm/vm_resident.c
index 040a1f9..704a601 100644
--- a/osfmk/vm/vm_resident.c
+++ b/osfmk/vm/vm_resident.c
@@ -775,6 +775,14 @@ vm_free_delayed_pages(void)
 		start_free_va = ((start_free_va + I386_LPGMASK) & ~I386_LPGMASK);
 	}
 #endif
+	if (vince_gap_end != 0) {
+		/*
+		 * vince: with the second bank the array is sized for the whole span, so the unused end
+		 * is a few hundred pages. ml_static_mfree() would hand them to the VM with their kernel
+		 * mappings still in the pv lists and pmap_assert_free() panics when they are reused.
+		 * Keep them (under a MiB).
+		 */
+	} else
 	if (start_free_va < (vm_offset_t)vm_page_array_ending_addr) {
 		free_size = trunc_page((vm_offset_t)vm_page_array_ending_addr - start_free_va);
 		if (free_size > 0) {
-- 
